`.map()` runs a function across every row of a dataset and returns a new dataset with the results — the ML equivalent of the `.apply()` method on a pandas Series from the data science course, but built to handle datasets far larger than memory.

```python
def tokenize_fn(example):
    return tokenizer(example["text"], truncation=True)

tokenized = dataset.map(tokenize_fn, batched=True)
```
